[5/6] run constraint tests (every bad insert must be rejected) …

Test context: trip 4925 (bus 1 , capacity 47 , driver 1 ) departs '2027-01-09 21:00:00+01'
Valid booking 180008 holds seat 1 for passenger 10001 and is paid ₦6,500

=====================================================================
                    CONSTRAINT TESTS (every bad row must be rejected)
=====================================================================
                          test                          | result |                                          database_said                                          
--------------------------------------------------------+--------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 1. UNIQUE seat: seat 1 sold again to another passenger | PASS   | duplicate key value violates unique constraint "booking_seat_unique"
 2. UNIQUE passenger: passenger 1 takes a 2nd seat      | PASS   | duplicate key value violates unique constraint "booking_one_passenger_per_trip"
 3a. trigger: seat number above bus capacity            | PASS   | Seat 48 is out of range for trip 4925 (bus 1 has capacity 47)
 3b. trigger + CHECK: seat 0 (below range)              | PASS   | Seat 0 is out of range for trip 4925 (bus 1 has capacity 47)
 4. trigger: booking made after the trip departed       | PASS   | Trip 4925 departed at 2027-01-09 21:00:00+01; a seat cannot be booked at 2027-01-09 22:00:00+01
 5. EXCLUDE bus overlap: same bus, overlapping time     | PASS   | conflicting key value violates exclusion constraint "trip_no_bus_overlap"
 6. EXCLUDE driver overlap: same driver, other bus      | PASS   | conflicting key value violates exclusion constraint "trip_no_driver_overlap"
 7. CHECK arrival after departure                       | PASS   | new row for relation "trip" violates check constraint "trip_arrival_after_departure"
 8a. CHECK route terminals differ: from = to            | PASS   | new row for relation "route" violates check constraint "route_diff_terminals"
 8b. UNIQUE route pair: same route twice                | PASS   | duplicate key value violates unique constraint "route_pair_unique"
 9a. CHECK route fare > 0: fare = -1                    | PASS   | new row for relation "route" violates check constraint "route_fare_pos"
 9b. CHECK payment > 0: amount = 0                      | PASS   | new row for relation "payment" violates check constraint "payment_amount_pos"
 10. UNIQUE payment.booking_id: second payment          | PASS   | duplicate key value violates unique constraint "payment_booking_id_key"
 11a. CHECK refund >= 0: refund = -1                    | PASS   | new row for relation "cancellation" violates check constraint "cancellation_refund_nonneg"
 11b. trigger: refund more than amount paid             | PASS   | Refund ₦9999.00 is more than the ₦6500.00 paid for booking 180008
 12. CHECK trip_window matches depart/arrive            | PASS   | new row for relation "trip" violates check constraint "trip_window_matches"
(16 rows)


Positive check: after booking 180008 was cancelled, seat 1 was resold to passenger 10002 (accepted, as it should be).
 booking_id | passenger_id | seat_number |  status   | payment_status 
------------+--------------+-------------+-----------+----------------
     180008 |        10001 |           1 | CANCELLED | REFUNDED
     180014 |        10002 |           1 | CONFIRMED | 
(2 rows)


Result: 16 of 16 bad inserts were rejected. (All test rows rolled back.)
